> what is the range of x squared for x an unsigned byte?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..249   (44 distinct values)
  values: 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64..65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121, 129, 132, 137, 144..145, ...
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> does x times 2 plus 1 overflow for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x*2 + 1
  ucas: wrap it
wrap analysis of it:
  2x   (i8)
      nuw fails: unsigned wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      nsw fails: signed wrap at 128 points, e.g. x=-128  <- UB in C; a compiler assumes it cannot happen
  2x + 1   (i8)
      nuw holds
      nsw holds (C requires it: signed overflow is UB)
  end to end: differs from the mathematical result at 128 points, e.g. x=-128
      exact for: -64..63
  over all 256 points of the domain
> is x times x the same as x squared for an unsigned byte x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x*x
  ucas: that(x: u8) = x^2
  ucas: equiv it that
it and that are equal on the domain of it (exhaustive)
> what are the critical points of x cubed minus 3x?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3 - 3*x
  ucas: crit it
critical points of it:
  it' = 3x^2 - 3
  x ≈ -1: local maximum, it = 2
  x ≈ 1: local minimum, it = -2
  searched [-10, 10] (default; give x a range)
> the derivative of sin x squared with respect to x?
  ucas: it(x) = sin(x^2)
  ucas: diff it x
d/dx it = 2x*cos(x^2)
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 3e-10)
> the integral of x squared times sin x from 0 to pi?
  ucas: it(x) = x^2*sin(x)
  ucas: integrate it from 0 to pi
∫ x^2*sin(x) dx
  = 2x*sin(x) + 2cos(x) - x^2*cos(x) + C
  check: d/dx of it equals the integrand at 401 points of [0, 3.14159] (max difference 8.9e-16)
  from 0 to 3.14159: F(3.14159) - F(0) = 5.86960440108936
  numeric (adaptive Gauss-Kronrod 7-15, 15 evaluations): 5.86960440108936, estimated error 6.5e-14
  the two agree to 0
> the sum of i squared for i from 1 to n?
  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  ucas: show it
it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  -> int
> the product of i for i from 1 to n?
  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)
  ucas: show it
it(n: int in 0..100) = prod(i, 1, n, i)
  -> int
> the closed form of the sum of i squared for i from 1 to n?
  ucas: it(n: int in 0..100) = sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  ucas: closed it
sum(i, 1, n, i^2)
  = n*(n + 1)*(2n + 1)/6
  method: Faulhaber (polynomial in the index)
  check: equals direct iteration at all 101 points of the domain
> find 2 cheaper implementations of x squared plus 1 for an unsigned byte x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2 + 1
  ucas: find it 2
find it: 256 points, computing in u8, costs from gt1030
  cost 3   x*x + 1                                  affine fit
  cost 4   x^2 + 1                                  polynomial (Horner)
  [searched every term up to cost 4: 65536 distinct columns, bank full; 'more' continues]
